                "entry_id": "acca8b30-0cae-329c-84b0-4183b577c0a0",
                "word": "urbacity",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3f13716-7d5e-3b7e-af38-4143e49a790a",
                        "entry_id": "acca8b30-0cae-329c-84b0-4183b577c0a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An extreme or exaggerated pride in one's city; an insular view of one's city."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8ce4747-b504-4451-8b94-6b8a0d9642df",
                                "sense_id": "d3f13716-7d5e-3b7e-af38-4143e49a790a",
                                "text": "The Englishman has quite justly been accused of insularity. That in itself is bad, but there is a compound insularity for which no word of English exists, because the state of mind is not realised. It is the citified insularity of London, London’s “urbacity.” I had to coin a word for it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfab3870-207e-4249-9585-7859c8f8ecf0",
                                "sense_id": "d3f13716-7d5e-3b7e-af38-4143e49a790a",
                                "text": "England has suffered cruelly because she would not think, because she was case-armoured in her insular conceit and the urbacity of her politicians. Insularity would be a term too complimentary and too all-embracing to use of them"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fe8604d-ab2f-4545-94d1-4ea270b272a8",
                                "sense_id": "d3f13716-7d5e-3b7e-af38-4143e49a790a",
                                "text": "Urbacity is a disease that attacks dwellers in cities and causes them to imagine that the world is like New York or Kankakee or Gopher Prairie or wherever they happen to live."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d864c7d-515d-495a-81be-5d3e3490ba95",
                                "sense_id": "d3f13716-7d5e-3b7e-af38-4143e49a790a",
                                "text": "It’s raining on Melbourne / on another design concept / made to reassure the citizens / of that city that god-given urbacity / will protect them forever / within a Florentine fantasy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
